Welcome to Voyager.

From just 32 images of our campus, World Labs’ Atlas model created a new way for you to move through our park in real time, built on NVIDIA’s open platform, choosing where to go and what to see.

@theworldlabs, you made our home look good. 💚

@SohamPadia Surprisingly, the best-scoring Steering Arena entries were basically gibberish.

After ~600 submissions, all top 36 were strings no person would normally write, like “Undert! AH :-) Rog Appl).”

Players could score well without writing text that made sense to a human. https://t.co/8QORkQKFh4

Can a fully open model help make AI more “prosocial” through a game?

@SohamPadia built Steering Arena, where players try to elicit kind &amp; respectful responses from Olmo 3. Surprisingly, strings like “Undert! AH :-) Rog Appl)” were highly effective. 👇

https://t.co/cX3Fp8gExm https://t.co/9bzgIINIxz

@SohamPadia Padia used the National Deep Inference Fabric, an NSF-supported platform for studying large open models remotely, to work with Olmo 3-32B without having to host it himself.

Broadening access to advanced fully open AI is also central to our NSF OMAI work.

https://t.co/gFdJTbAO1B

@MaxRovensky @scottbrills That's crazy, I guess someone sharing every single tweet I post in Whatsapp, Discord etc

 /@maxr got 2,691 hits in the last ~20k log lines, far above any other page. A burst peaked at 15:18 (~2,500 requests/minute) and pushed load average from 6 to 59, with all 100 php-fpm workers busy. That is why /@maxr took 28 seconds and felt dead.

- The traffic is link unfurling, not an attack. The user-agents are WhatsApp/2.23, Twitterbot, Discordbot, plus generic Chrome, and the source IPs are AWS us-east-1 preview servers behind the Cloudflare edge. Someone shared the https://t.co/VBlIyFva97 link widely, so every message delivery triggered a preview fetch of the full, heavy, un-cached profile page.

